! b6-exports-homes-bridge — Reader-Six: Lares (Tasked Spirit)
Read 2026-10-31 against main checkout HEAD 27bc0cb6b (+ the untracked test-recut-road.mem). Personas: Ink-Clerk (grounds), Map-Wisp (consequence path). Read-only; one report file.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/findings`>>

!! FINDINGS (security / fail-open candidates)

F-1 (medium, identity drift; fails toward a SECOND identity, not open): `readLocalOperatorHint` (packages/lararium-node/src/node-vessel-identity.ts:124) shells `git config --global user.email|user.name` with a 2 s timeout, swallows every error, and its `login` slug NAMES THE CUSTODY FILES: `.vessel-key-<login>.json`, the KEL file, the staged-rotation file, and every persona-root row (`keyFileName`, `kelFileName`, `stagedFileName`, `personaGroupRootFileName(login, …)`). Eleven call sites wrap it `.catch(() => ({login:null,…}))` (dead catch: the function never rejects). Consequences measured by reading: (a) a git timeout under load, a daemon started with no HOME / another HOME / `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL` set, or an edited global email makes the SAME vessel read `login = null` or a new slug, so it looks for `.vessel-key.json` instead of `.vessel-key-josh.json`; the loaders refuse "no key file … run lares vessel found", but `generateOrLoadVesselIdentity` (:856) mints a fresh key under the new name when it holds custody. (b) Different callers in one process can read different logins mid-run (only `placeReadingWatch` :337 freezes it "once, at the first read"; `loadPlaceKelChain`, `loadPlaceReading`, `loadPlaceAid`, `rotatePlace`, `reconcilePlaceRotation` each re-shell). Not a key-to-surface leak; it is mutable ambient host state deciding which key a vessel is. It bites the "custody read by capability, never host" law directly. Cure sits in T16 below: resolve the login ONCE at open, record it in the identity dir (or drop the login-suffixed names), inject it.

F-2 (low, note): `verifyWaxStampSig` (mesh/src/wax-stamp.ts:498) is the only verifier of a wax-stamp signature. It has no production caller and NO test (token appears once in the tree). `mintWaxStamp` has no production caller either. No consumer exists to fail open today; road W30 owes the live equivocation plane. Whoever wires stamps must not consume `WaxStamp` without it. Red-first test is owed before any wiring.

F-3 (low, unproven): `cabalInviteId` (mesh/src/cabal-invite.ts:171) docstring promises "a seen-cache, so one vouch admits one joiner one time". No seen-cache consumes it. I did not trace whether one-use rides the epoch bound instead; whoever opens the dead-export lane should read cabal-vouch/cabal-join for that before deleting.

