! T4 — the dead exports

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/method`>>

!! Method (regenerated, not copied)
The scout's script text is not on disk (final.md holds only the count). I regenerated: every `export (function|const|let|class|interface|type|enum)` under packages/*/src (8,385 declarations); a token index over every tracked-or-untracked, non-ignored text file in the workspace (`git ls-files -co`, files under 5 MB: src, tests, tools, scripts, `.tid`, `.mem`, `.md`, `.json`, `.py`, generated plugin files). A name is DEAD when its token occurs exactly ONCE in the whole tree (its declaration). That catches comments, `.mem`, `.tid`, string-keyed spellings of the identifier, and dynamic `import()` sites naming it. Result: ''67 names'' (not 53; the scout's 53 used another counting rule and the tree has moved). Classes also found:
* 1,089 names occur only in their declaring file (exported but used locally: an "unexport" class, not dead; out of scope).
* 487 names occur nowhere but a package `index.ts` (the barrel class, below).
Hidden-consumer sweeps run: string values (`holder:admitted`, `daemon:face-*`, `cas-want-have`, `sibling/*`, tags, filename patterns), package.json `exports` subpaths, `export *` barrels, road/kit `.mem` for owed consumers.

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/public-surface-caveat`>>

!! PUBLIC-SURFACE CAVEAT (changes the lean for ~30 names)
<code>&#64;lararium/mesh</code>, `mempalace` and `sensorium` index.ts use `export * from "./x.js"`; mesh also publishes subpaths (record-port, ffz-project, lar-uris, mirror-paths, face-proof-subjects, session-contract). A name with zero consumers there is still PUBLIC API of a shared cap-stack package that browser vessels import. <code>&#64;lararium/node</code> publishes only `.` with named export lists, so its unlisted names are private. "Delete the 53" therefore changes the d.ts surface of mesh; `tools/evergreen-boundary.mjs` and the typecheck witness are the instruments, and the operator should know the mesh names are API cuts.

