!! Cut risks (whole batch)
* Mesh deletions change the published d.ts of a shared package; one batch, announced after a controller land.
* In-flight collisions: u1 touches content-key-seat, operator-daemon-behavior, content-key-holder, session-sign-door (no overlap with the 67). ralias touches face-fleet-view.ts, kahu-realm.ts, open-node-vessel.ts, realm-bag.ts, protected-doc-guard.ts (no overlap with the 67 either; none of my names live in those files).
* Typecheck is blind to string-keyed use; the token index already covers it, but re-run it the day the lane opens (185 commits a month).
* Red-first: delete one name that keeps a consumer in a scratch tree and prove the typecheck witness reds before trusting a zero; plant a known-dead name as the control.

