<<~ ahu slot=`#/t16-the-home-and-env-reads`>>

! T16 — the home and env reads (injected homes)

<<~/ahu>>

<<~ ahu slot=`#/what-readlocaloperatorhint-is`>>

!! What `readLocalOperatorHint` is (node-vessel-identity.ts:124-141, read whole)
Async, module-private. Runs `git config --global user.name` and `… user.email` through `promisify(execFile)`, 2 s timeout each, catches everything, returns `{ login, displayName }`. `login` = email local-part, non-alnum to `-`, lower-cased. State read: the child process's env (HOME, XDG_CONFIG_HOME, GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL, PATH) and the host's global git file. Writes none. Clock: the 2 s timeout is a wall-clock decision (a "no global now" tension: a slow `git` flips the answer).
Callers (all in node-vessel-identity.ts): :315 reconcilePlaceRotation, :322 loadPlaceKelChain, :328 loadPlaceReading, :343 placeReadingWatch (reads once, keeps), :356 loadPlaceAid, :364 rotatePlace, :420 generateOrLoadVesselIdentity, :492 loadVesselIdentity (displayName), :523 loadVesselVerifyingKey, :540 loadVesselSigningSeed, :583 vesselFloorKeyDoor, :856 makeNodeFsPersonaVault (once per vault), :882 loginHint. Thirteen call sites, each a fresh pair of shell-outs.
Uses of `login`: file NAMES (`keyFileName`, `kelFileName`, `stagedFileName`, `personaGroupRootFileName`, roster rows) and the `gitEmail` informational field in the persisted key. `displayName` feeds `VesselIdentity.displayName` (IdentityTiddler enrichment only).
Tests: `hermetic-git-global.test.ts`, `node-vessel-identity-sealed.test.ts:89-100` and `place-rotation.test.ts:47-67` each set `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL`/`HOME`/`XDG_CONFIG_HOME` by hand; `tests/support/scratch-custody-setup.ts:33` sets `GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null` process-wide for every node suite (so the hint reads `null` in every suite: the login-suffixed path is exercised by only the few tests that plant a config).

