SAFETY note on `readBackStandsIn` (seal-ceremony.ts:337): a product path decides "the person read their cold cards" from an env var plus a file marker plus a proof under a published passphrase. The code already hardens it (marker alone insufficient; custody must prove under the published test route, spending an unlock attempt on a miss), so I do not file it as a fault. It is host-ambient state steering a ceremony and belongs in the injected record: `{ readBack: "person" | "standsIn" }` decided at the opener, not by env.

